# ApexForge - Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values
# Note: This application uses runtime configuration via Spark SDK
# Most settings are configured through the UI, not environment variables

# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION NOTES
# =============================================================================
# - No environment variables are required for basic functionality
# - API keys are managed through the application UI
# - CEO credentials are stored securely in the codebase (not in .env)
# - All sensitive data uses the Spark KV storage system
# =============================================================================

# Development Mode (automatically detected by Vite)
# NODE_ENV=development  # Set by Vite automatically

# Build Configuration
# VITE_APP_TITLE=ApexForge
# VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# =============================================================================
# USER-PROVIDED CONFIGURATION (via UI)
# =============================================================================
# The following are configured through the application interface:
# - AI Provider API Keys (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.)
# - Stripe API Keys
# - Email Service Keys (Resend)
# - SMS Service Keys (Twilio)
# - Figma Access Tokens
# - Webhook Configuration

# =============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# =============================================================================
# - Never commit actual API keys to version control
# - CEO credentials are NOT stored in environment variables
# - Use the application's secure KV storage for sensitive data
# - IP whitelist is managed through the CEO dashboard
# =============================================================================
